.md
## Output forms

An output form answers a different question from `Style` or `Grid`: it chooses
the representation used to display an expression.

### `StandardForm`: normal WLJS output

[`StandardForm`](./../Formatting/StandardForm) is the default form for ordinary
Wolfram Language output cells. In WLJS it is implemented as decorated
[`InputForm`](./../Formatting/InputForm): comments carry visual metadata for
fractions, grids, and other structures, while the remaining text is still valid
Wolfram Language input.

For example, a visually typeset fraction remains based on the plain expression
`(1)/(2)`. This is why WLJS notebook code works well with text editors, Git, and
LLM tools. See [Math typesetting and shortcuts](./../Overview#math-typesetting-and-shortcuts)
for the editor-side details.

You rarely need to write `StandardForm` explicitly in a normal output cell. It
is useful when an expression is being inserted into a cell type that normally
uses another form:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Output forms

An output form answers a different question from `Style` or `Grid`: it chooses
the representation used to display an expression.

### `StandardForm`: normal WLJS output

[`StandardForm`](./../Formatting/StandardForm) is the default form for ordinary
Wolfram Language output cells. In WLJS it is implemented as decorated
[`InputForm`](./../Formatting/InputForm): comments carry visual metadata for
fractions, grids, and other structures, while the remaining text is still valid
Wolfram Language input.

For example, a visually typeset fraction remains based on the plain expression
`(1)/(2)`. This is why WLJS notebook code works well with text editors, Git, and
LLM tools. See [Math typesetting and shortcuts](./../Overview#math-typesetting-and-shortcuts)
for the editor-side details.

You rarely need to write `StandardForm` explicitly in a normal output cell. It
is useful when an expression is being inserted into a cell type that normally
uses another form:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
expr = Panel[1/2];
expr
StandardForm[expr]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*BB[*)(Panel[(*FB[*)((1)(*,*)/(*,*)(2))(*]FB*)])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNiYGAo5gcSAUX5ZZkpqSn+BSWZ+XnFaYwgCV4gEZaZWu6SmpxflFiSXxTMClKamJeaA9HJAiSCSnNSg0EMj9TEFIQCAH5qF00="*)(*]BB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*BB[*)(Panel[(*FB[*)((1)(*,*)/(*,*)(2))(*]FB*)])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNiYGAo5gcSAUX5ZZkpqSn+BSWZ+XnFaYwgCV4gEZaZWu6SmpxflFiSXxTMClKamJeaA9HJAiSCSnNSg0EMj9TEFIQCAH5qF00="*)(*]BB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
### `InputForm`: inspect the underlying expression

[`InputForm`](./../Formatting/InputForm) displays a one-dimensional
representation close to what you would type in a source file:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
### `InputForm`: inspect the underlying expression

[`InputForm`](./../Formatting/InputForm) displays a one-dimensional
representation close to what you would type in a source file:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Red

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(RGBColor[1, 0, 0])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNiYGAo5gUSYZmp5S6pyflFiSX5RcEsQBHn4PCQNGaQPAeQCHJ3cs7PyS8qYgCDD/ZQBgMDnAEA4iUPRg=="*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md


%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%


%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Red // InputForm

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(InputForm[RGBColor[1, 0, 0]])(*,*)(*"1:"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
The first result is shown as a color. The second exposes its underlying
expression:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
The first result is shown as a color. The second exposes its underlying
expression:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
To obtain that representation as a string, use the two-argument form of
`ToString`:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
To obtain that representation as a string, use the two-argument form of
`ToString`:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
ToString[Red, InputForm]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
"RGBColor[1, 0, 0]"

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
