.md
`InputForm` is especially useful for debugging unfamiliar symbolic objects,
copying an expression to a plain-text environment, or seeing what a visual
decoration contains.

### `TraditionalForm`: mathematical notation

[`TraditionalForm`](./../Formatting/TraditionalForm) displays expressions using
conventional mathematical notation:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
`InputForm` is especially useful for debugging unfamiliar symbolic objects,
copying an expression to a plain-text environment, or seeing what a visual
decoration contains.

### `TraditionalForm`: mathematical notation

[`TraditionalForm`](./../Formatting/TraditionalForm) displays expressions using
conventional mathematical notation:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Series[Sin[x], {x, 0, 7}] // TraditionalForm

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(Null)(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRAeO5AISY0Iy0wtRwj4p6Xl5CdCVXACidAgH5fU5PyU1OASIK9CV9XUOa0oMVnV3KlC1dTVWNXcBcg0A1FGTqhyphA5QyMDIANNnzlEztTAxACi1R8on5OaVqJqZAGStwByizLTM4B8SwADMS0N"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
